<node>
    <node name="description" channel="inline" format="text/plain" model="A complex number written in polar form with absolute value and argument, whereby the argument representing an exponent is encapsulated by the sequence &#x0022;exp()&#x0022;.

Caution! The i (or j in electrical engineering) in the exponent is neglected, so that -2*exp(i45) is written without i or j as -2*exp(45) in cybol.

The complex number given in trigonometric form:
2 (cos 30° + i sin 30°)
which can also be written in exponential form, using Euler&#x0027;s formula:
2 e ^(i 30)
would be written in CYBOL as:
2*exp(30)

-2*exp(-45)"/>
    <node name="examples" channel="file" format="text/plain" model="api-generator/spec/state/number/complex-polar/examples.txt"/>
</node>
